  double(own n: Int) -> Int
  add(ref x: a) -> a with Mutate
    with !Alloc (declared)
      The feedback, <~, adds each number to the total before it.
      `!Alloc` is checked on every build: a version
      of this stage that allocates does not build.
  bar(own n: Int) -> String with Alloc + Memory + MemoryWrite + Address + Diverge + Trap
  say(own n: a, own b: b) with Alloc + Memory + MemoryWrite + Address + Console
  row(ref x: Int) with Mutate + Alloc + Memory + MemoryWrite + Address + Console + Diverge + Trap
      The share, <|, sends each total to two stages, and
      the pipe, |>, hands both answers to `say`.
  main() -> Int with Alloc + Address + Memory + MemoryWrite + Diverge + Trap + Mutate + WASI
      The install, ~>, sends what `print` writes to the screen.
